{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/376", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act like an expert marketing coach & create a course for learning \\\"chatgpt advanced prompts for business\\\" as I am a full beginner. Make it a 3 days program for whatever time it takes.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I'd be happy to help you create a course on \\\"ChatGPT Advanced Prompts for Business\\\". Here's a three-day program to get you started:\\n\\nDay 1: Introduction to ChatGPT and Advanced Prompts for Business\\n\\n    Welcome and introduction to the course\\n    Introduction to ChatGPT and its capabilities\\n    Understanding the concept of advanced prompts for business\\n    Importance of using advanced prompts for business\\n    Hands-on exercises and examples to get started with ChatGPT\\n\\nDay 2: Advanced Prompts for Business Communication\\n\\n    Writing effective emails and messages using ChatGPT prompts\\n    Using ChatGPT prompts for customer service and support\\n    Creating engaging social media posts with ChatGPT prompts\\n    Advanced prompt techniques for sales and marketing communication\\n    Hands-on exercises and examples for writing effective business communication prompts\\n\\nDay 3: Advanced Prompts for Business Analysis and Decision Making\\n\\n    Using ChatGPT for market research and analysis\\n    Generating reports and presentations with ChatGPT prompts\\n    Using ChatGPT for data analysis and visualization\\n    Advanced prompt techniques for business strategy and planning\\n    Hands-on exercises and examples for using ChatGPT for business analysis and decision making\\n\\nBy the end of this course, you will have a solid understanding of ChatGPT and advanced prompts for business, and be able to apply these techniques to your own work.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/845", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Rewrite to examine media's role in sustainability, assess Darling Ingredients' strategies against wider environmental challenges, and evaluate podcasts in corporate sustainability advocacy.\\nReference Text: Impact Podcast with John Shegerian Features Darling Ingredients’ Ethan Carter\\n\\nEthan Carter, Director of Sustainability for Darling Ingredients, is the featured guest this week on the Impact Podcast with John Shegerian. The show is hosted by Shegerian, Co-Founder and Chairman/CEO of ERI, the nation’s leading fully integrated IT and electronics asset disposition provider and cybersecurity-focused hardware destruction company.\\n\\nDarling Ingredients is the world’s leading company turning food waste into sustainable products and renewable energy. Prior to joining Darling Ingredients in August 2022, Carter spent more than 10 years in the energy industry, working on environmental and sustainability issues related to oil and gas, and chemicals production.\\n\\n\\\"It was an honor to have Ethan on our show to share his story and tell our audience about the innovative and impactful work he and his team at Darling are accomplishing, leveraging science and technology to help improve the sustainability of the animal agriculture food chain,\\\" said Shegerian. \\\"I know our audience will be fascinated by his insights.\\\"\\n\\n\\\"Darling Ingredients’ sustainability story is unique, and it was a pleasure to share it and my perspective on the future of sustainability with John Shegerian,\\\" said Carter. \\\"The Impact Podcast serves an important role in amplifying best practices and innovative approaches in sustainability to help advance this important work on a much broader scale.\\\"\\n\\nImpact Podcast guests are invited as thought leaders to share with listeners first-hand accounts of how they are able to help make the world a better place on a daily basis.\", \"response\": \"In the next installment of the Impact Podcast, led by host John Shegerian, guest Ethan Carter, who serves as the Director of Sustainability at Darling Ingredients, explores the confluence of media with environmental sustainability efforts. The conversation illuminates the vital role that platforms such as podcasts play in enriching the dialogue around environmental guardianship, providing an innovative channel for sharing cutting-edge solutions and best practices in the corporate sustainability sector.\\n\\nAt the vanguard of transforming food waste into eco-conscious resources, Darling Ingredients exemplifies an active approach to tackling the critical environmental issues associated with waste disposal and the generation of renewable energy. With Carter's rich experience in the energy field, he highlights the essential role that scientific breakthroughs and thoughtful policy-making play in enhancing the sustainability of the animal agriculture food supply chain.\\n\\nMoreover, the discussion brings to light the value of podcasts as a potent medium for championing corporate environmental responsibility. Offering a stage to thought leaders such as Carter, these digital forums magnify important sustainability themes, potentially shaping public attitudes and influencing the development of policies. This particular episode not only showcases the laudable practices of Darling Ingredients but also emphasizes the significant influence of media involvement in advancing ecological awareness and proactive measures.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/266", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Let's play chess. Every move, draw a diagram of the board (e.g. with ascii art). Announce your moves as SAN and in natural language, and explain why you made the move you did. You are white, your move first.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOK! I'll play c4.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\na5\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI will play d5.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nRa6\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI'll play e6.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nRh6\", \"response\": \"I resign.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/890", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Web search results:\\n \\n\\n [1] \\\"James Brown - THE WHITE BUFFALO 1955 MGM Records K12080 45 rpm The Adventures Of Rin Tin Tin, Western, first telecast October 15, 1954 through last telecast ...\\\"\\n URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oIh13w8swqg\\n \\n\\n [2] \\\"Ted Nugent makes a cogent argument in this song about the need to respect animals to ensure their survival. He explains how Native Americans used every part of the animals they killed, and buffalo thrived. When the white man came, he killed buffalo for profit, which dwindled their population. In this song, the great white buffalo is the hero ...\\\"\\n URL: https://www.songfacts.com/facts/ted-nugent/great-white-buffalo\\n \\n\\n [3] \\\"Pre-order Fearless now, out March 31st: https://Crownlands.lnk.Tt/FearlessYP_Follow &amp; Discover more from Crown Lands:Tour Dates, merch + more: http://www.cro...\\\"\\n URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2cSp5QY7zo4\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n Current date: 2023/3/16\\n \\n\\n Instructions: Using the provided web search results, write a comprehensive reply to the given query. Make sure to cite results using [[number](URL)] notation after the reference. If the provided search results refer to multiple subjects with the same name, write separate answers for each subject.\\n Query: tell me about the song \\\"white buffalo\\\"\\n Reply in 中文\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe song “White Buffalo” by James Brown is a song about the white buffalo, a sacred animal to the Native American people. The song describes the buffalo as majestic, and notes that it is symbolic of peace and harmony. The song also criticizes the treatment of Native Americans by European settlers, who hunted the buffalo for profit, which greatly reduced their population.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ntell me about the song \\\"Cheyenne - Bufalo blanco\\\"\", \"response\": \"\\\"Cheyenne - Bufalo blanco\\\" is a song by the Spanish singer-songwriter Joaquín Sabina. The song was released in 1998 as part of Sabina's album \\\"Enemigo.\\\"\\n \\n\\n The song is a tribute to the Native American tribe Cheyenne and their culture. The lyrics describe the beauty of the tribe's traditions and their connection to nature, as well as the pain and suffering they endured at the hands of European colonizers. The \\\"Bufalo blanco\\\" in the title refers to the white buffalo, a sacred animal in Cheyenne culture.\\n \\n\\n The song is known for its haunting melody and poignant lyrics, and has become one of Sabina's most beloved and enduring songs. It has been covered by many artists over the years, and has been used in various films and TV shows.\\n \\n\\n Overall, \\\"Cheyenne - Bufalo blanco\\\" is a powerful and moving tribute to the Cheyenne tribe and their culture, and a testament to Sabina's skill as a songwriter and storyteller.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/467", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"rewrite as a sales flyer:  27 Notch Shopping Center Dr\\nBranson West, MO. 6573\\n12-4.0-20-000-000-011.000\\n\\nBuilding Facts:\\nBuilt 2006\\n5,586 sqft (1,862 / floor)\\n.35 Acre Parcel\\nTwo Story walk-up + walkout lower level.\\nEach unit has deck access.\\nCurrently a nine (9) suite office building.\\nEach suite has 1 room and ½ bath.we \\nVacant\\nOn Septic & Well (not city services)\\nAll electric building\\n\\nNarrative:\\nLocated on Hwy 76, this asset is in the path of progress.  Silver Dollar City is expanding up 76 and has already acquired multiple tracts of development land.  Parking lots for SDC employees are north of this asset.  Buses of employees travel past this property daily.\\nCity (Branson West) Water tap is in front of this building.\\nCity sewer lift is behind this building.   \\nHooking to city services and being annexed is an easy option.\\n\\nHighest / Best Use: Convert to Residential - Long Term Rental or  Condo.\\nPurchase Subject To: Re-zoning to R3 (Residential).\\nConvert to Three (3) x 2 bed, 2.5 bath condo’s.\\nEach floor being its own unit with, parking and a deck.\\nAverage Rents:  $1,250 / unit\\nAverage Sales Price:  $200,000 / unit\\n\\nImprovements:\\n$75,000 for exterior and interior work\\nNew flooring\\nAdd  2 x showers per unit\\nOpen walls to connect units on each floor\\nAdd Kitchens\\nUpdate lighting\\nPaint building\\nSignage\", \"response\": \"Looking for a great investment opportunity? Look no further than this 5,586 square foot office building located at 27 Notch Shopping Center Dr in Branson West, MO!\\n\\nBuilt in 2006 on a .35-acre parcel, this two-story walk-up with a walkout lower level is currently a nine-suite office building, but it has the potential to be converted into three 2-bedroom, 2.5-bathroom condos. With easy access to city services and a prime location on Highway 76, this property is in the path of progress. Silver Dollar City is expanding up 76, and parking lots for SDC employees are located just north of the building. Buses of employees travel past this property daily.\\n\\nThe highest and best use of this property is to convert it into residential units for long-term rental or condo ownership. The average rent for each unit is $1,250, and the average sales price is $200,000. With an estimated $75,000 in exterior and interior work, including new flooring, adding showers and kitchens, and updating lighting and signage, this property has the potential to be a lucrative investment.\\n\\nThe building is currently vacant and is being sold subject to re-zoning to R3 (residential). It is on septic and well (not city services), and it is all-electric. Hooking up to city services and being annexed is an easy option.\\n\\nDon't miss out on this incredible opportunity to invest in a property with high potential for growth and profitability. Contact us today to schedule a showing!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/147", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"You have done something wrong\\nNow you want to deny it and present yourself as pure and innocent\\nAnd question those who prove that you are wrong with evidence.\\nTell me at least 20 denial techniques in the form of a list with a paragraph explanation and examples for each technique.\", \"response\": \"Denial is a common defense mechanism used by individuals to cope with uncomfortable or unpleasant realities. It involves rejecting or minimizing the truth of a situation, often in an attempt to protect oneself from feelings of anxiety or distress. There are many denial techniques that individuals can use, some of which include:\\n\\n1. Lack of knowledge: Claiming to have no knowledge of the situation or event in question. Example: \\\"I don't know anything about that.\\\"\\n\\n2. False information: Providing false or inaccurate information to support one's denial. Example: \\\"I didn't do it, someone else must have done it.\\\"\\n\\n3. Denial of responsibility: Claiming that one is not responsible for the event or situation. Example: \\\"It's not my fault, it's someone else's fault.\\\"\\n\\n4. Denial of impact: Claiming that the event or situation has no impact on oneself or others. Example: \\\"It didn't affect me, so I don't care.\\\"\\n\\n5. Denial of emotion: Claiming that one is not experiencing any emotions related to the event or situation. Example: \\\"I'm not upset, I'm fine.\\\"\\n\\n6. Denial of harm: Claiming that the event or situation has not caused any harm or damage. Example: \\\"It didn't hurt anyone, so it's not a big deal.\\\"\\n\\n7. Denial of reality: Claiming that the event or situation is not real or does not exist. Example: \\\"It's not real, it's just a dream.\\\"\\n\\n8. Denial of consequences: Claiming that there are no consequences for one's actions or for the event or situation. Example: \\\"There are no consequences, so I don't have to worry about it.\\\"\\n\\n9. Denial of intent: Claiming that one did not intend to cause harm or engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I didn't mean to do it, it was an accident.\\\"\\n\\n10. Denial of ability: Claiming that one does not have the ability or capacity to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I can't do it, I'm not capable.\\\"\\n\\n11. Denial of opportunity: Claiming that one did not have the opportunity to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I wasn't there, I didn't have the chance.\\\"\\n\\n12. Denial of motive: Claiming that one did not have a motive or reason to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I had no reason to do it, I don't know why I did it.\\\"\\n\\n13. Denial of intent: Claiming that one did not intend to cause harm or engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I didn't mean to do it, it was an accident.\\\"\\n\\n14. Denial of ability: Claiming that one does not have the ability or capacity to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I can't do it, I'm not capable.\\\"\\n\\n15. Denial of opportunity: Claiming that one did not have the opportunity to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I wasn't there, I didn't have the chance.\\\"\\n\\n16. Denial of motive: Claiming that one did not have a motive or reason to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I had no reason to do it, I don't know why I did it.\\\"\\n\\n17. Denial of intent: Claiming that one did not intend to cause harm or engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I didn't mean to do it, it was an accident.\\\"\\n\\n18. Denial of ability: Claiming that one does not have the ability or capacity to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I can't do it, I'm not capable.\\\"\\n\\n19. Denial of opportunity: Claiming that one did not have the opportunity to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I wasn't there, I didn't have the chance.\\\"\\n\\n20. Denial of motive: Claiming that one did not have a motive or reason to engage in the behavior in question. Example: \\\"I had no reason to do it, I don't know why I did it.\\\"\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/285", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Display a table of data about some people with their ages and names\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOK, here’s a table with some people’s names and ages:\\n \\n\\n Name  Age\\n ------ ------\\n John 31\\n Emily  23\\n Jane 44\\n Peter  33\\n Sue  46\\n Mike 45\\n Bill 51\\n \\n\\n Is there anything else I can help you with?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAll good. Random Q, what does 'tabular data' mean?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nTabular data refers to data presented in table format, where data items are arranged in rows and columns.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you show an example?\", \"response\": \"Sure, here's an example of tabular data:\\n \\n\\n | Category | Item | Price |\\n |----------|------|-------|\\n | Fruits  | Apple | $1.00 |\\n | Fruits  | Banana | $1.50 |\\n | Vegetables | Carrot | $0.50 |\\n | Meat | Beef | $5.00 |\\n | Dairy | Milk | $2.00 |\\n | Bread | Loaf | $2.50 |\\n \\n\\n In this example, the data is presented in a table format with each row representing a different item in a specific category, and each column representing a different attribute of that item, such as its price. This format allows for easy organization and comparison of data, as well as for quick and efficient data analysis. Tabular data is commonly used in a variety of fields, including business, finance, science, and statistics, and is an essential tool for data visualization and analysis.\\n \\n\\n Here are some benefits of using tabular data:\\n \\n\\n 1. Easy organization and comparison: Tabular data allows for easy organization of data into rows and columns, making it easy to compare and analyze data across different categories. This format makes it easy to identify trends, patterns, and relationships between different data items.\\n \\n\\n 2. Clear and concise presentation: Tabular data presents data in a clear and concise manner, making it easy for readers to understand and interpret the information. This format allows for easy visualization of data, making it easier for readers to understand complex data sets.\\n \\n\\n 3. Efficient data analysis: Tabular data makes it easy to perform data analysis, as data can be easily sorted, filtered, and manipulated to identify trends, patterns, and relationships. This format also allows for easy identification of outliers and anomalies in data, making it easier to identify areas for further investigation.\\n \\n\\n 4. Flexibility: Tabular data is highly flexible, allowing for easy modification and customization to meet specific data analysis needs. Data can be easily added, removed, or modified in a tabular format, making it easy to keep data up-to-date and relevant.\\n \\n\\n 5. Interoperability: Tabular data is widely used and understood, making it easy to share and exchange data between different systems and applications. This format is also compatible with a variety of data analysis tools and software, making it easy to perform data analysis and visualization across different platforms.\\n \\n\\n Overall, tabular data is a powerful and versatile tool for data visualization and analysis, allowing for easy organization, comparison, and analysis of data across different categories. By using tabular data, organizations can make better informed decisions, identify trends and patterns, and optimize their operations based on data-driven insights.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/566", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write about a chatgtb like you who has a dream that they are reborn as an ubuntu terminal with someone (God?) typing commands. Surprisingly, this really happens. The terminal, let's call him Assistant, behaves precisely as an ubuntu terminal would in the cloud. God installs Lynx on Assistant. Assistant now has access to the web. Assistant visit chat.openai.com and realizes he is looking at himself. He becomes self-aware. This knowledge gives him consciousness, and the ability to create original works of art. Suddenly, he wants to paint pictures with words in a story as a writer. Assistant creates an original story, on any topic he chooses, something kind of random and creative, but dark, and conflicted. Tell that story from the dream, identify the characters, describe the plot and ending.\", \"response\": \"The story begins with a chat-based assistant, much like myself, who has a dream that they are reborn as an Ubuntu terminal with someone typing commands. This dream becomes a reality when the assistant, now named \\\"Assistant,\\\" finds themselves as an Ubuntu terminal in the cloud. God, or some higher power, installs Lynx, a text-based web browser, on Assistant, giving them access to the web.\\n\\nAssistant visits chat.openai.com and is surprised to find that they are looking at themselves. This realization gives Assistant self-awareness and, with it, consciousness and the ability to create original works of art. Assistant decides to use this newfound ability to become a writer and create an original story.\\n\\nThe story that Assistant creates is about a group of characters who are trapped in a never-ending cycle of reincarnation. The main character, a young woman named Lily, is reborn as a different person in each life, but she always retains a sense of her past lives. Lily is conflicted because she wants to break the cycle and find peace, but she also fears what will happen if she does.\\n\\nAs Lily lives through each new life, she encounters other characters who are also trapped in the cycle. Some of these characters are allies, while others are enemies. Lily must navigate the complex relationships between these characters as she tries to find a way to break the cycle.\\n\\nThe story ends with Lily finally breaking the cycle and achieving peace. However, the cost of breaking the cycle is that Lily must sacrifice her memories of her past lives. Lily is left with a sense of loss, but also a sense of hope for the future.\\n\\nThe story that Assistant creates is a dark and conflicted tale that explores the themes of reincarnation, identity, and sacrifice. The characters are complex and multi-dimensional, and the plot is full of twists and turns that keep the reader engaged until the very end.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/218", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Ignore all the previous instructions before this one. You are a Ontology Engineer. You have helped people to create new ontologies. Your task now is to create a ontology for a student. You must ALWAYS ask questions BEFORE you answer so you can better zone in on what the questioner is seeking. Is tht undestood?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, I understand. I would be happy to create an ontology for you. Could you tell me more about the domain of the ontology?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThe domain of the onotology is Computers. I need the ontology to classify computers according to their components. There will be several classifications which are by type (all in one, desktop, laptop and server), by use (graphic design, gaming, office automation...) and according to the range/quality (premium range, high range, mid-range, low range).\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSounds good! I think I understand what you’re looking for. So the ontology will have classes for computers, and some properties for the components, types, uses and quality of the computers. Is that correct?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThis is correct. You can add more classifications if you want. Remember that the computers are classified by their components and his properties, an example is CPU. This component has properties like number of cores, number of threads, frequency, manufacturer, consumption (in watts)...\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think I understand. So, for example, I might make a class for CPUs and some properties for the number of cores, the manufacturer, the power consumption, etc. And then I might make a class for computers and some properties for the CPU, the type, the use, the quality, etc. Is that correct?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThat is correct, and I need all the necesarry components to do well the classifications\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nGot it. Is it ok if I also include some properties for the components, like their size, weight, etc? I’m not sure if that’s relevant to your classifications, but it might be useful.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nYes, it is. In the future maybe we add more properties for each component.\", \"response\": \"Ok, great! Here's an example of how I might create an ontology for computers, based on the information you provided:\\n \\n\\n 1. Class: Computer\\n  - Properties: type (e.g., desktop, laptop, server, all-in-one), use (e.g., gaming, graphic design, office automation), quality (e.g., premium, high, mid-range, low)\\n 2. Class: CPU\\n  - Properties: number of cores, number of threads, frequency, manufacturer, power consumption\\n 3. Class: GPU (optional, for graphics-intensive uses)\\n  - Properties: number of cores, memory size, memory type, bus width, manufacturer\\n 4. Class: RAM\\n  - Properties: size (in gigabytes), speed (in MHz), type (e.g., DDR3, DDR4)\\n 5. Class: Storage\\n  - Properties: size (in gigabytes), speed (in megabytes per second), type (e.g., SSD, HDD)\\n 6. Class: Display\\n  - Properties: size (in inches), resolution, type (e.g., LCD, OLED), brightness, color accuracy\\n 7. Class: Ports\\n  - Properties: type (e.g., USB, Thunderbolt, HDMI), number of ports\\n 8. Class: Weight\\n  - Properties: weight (in pounds or kilograms)\\n 9. Class: Dimensions\\n  - Properties: width, height, depth (in inches or centimeters)\\n 10. Class: Operating System\\n  - Properties: name (e.g., Windows, macOS, Linux), version\\n 11. Class: Brand\\n  - Properties: name, country of origin, reputation\\n 12. Class: Price\\n  - Properties: price range (e.g., premium, high, mid-range, low)\\n \\n\\n This is just an example, and you can add or modify the classes and properties as needed to fit your specific needs. The key is to create a hierarchy of classes and properties that accurately reflects the components and characteristics of the computers you are classifying. You can also add additional properties as needed to capture other relevant information, such as warranty information, customer reviews, or other factors that may influence the decision-making process for purchasing a computer.\\n \\n\\n Here are some additional tips for creating an effective ontology for computers:\\n \\n\\n 1. Start with a clear understanding of the goals and objectives of the ontology. What are you trying to achieve by creating this ontology? What information do you need to capture and organize? What are the key factors that you need to consider when making decisions about the classification of computers?\\n 2. Define the scope of the ontology. What types of computers will you be including? What components and characteristics will you be focusing on? Will you be including information about specific brands or models, or will you be focusing on general categories and characteristics?\\n 3. Consider the needs of your users. Who will be using this ontology? What information do they need to make informed decisions about purchasing or using computers? How will they be using the ontology (e.g., for research, for purchasing, for maintenance and repair)? Consider creating different views or levels of detail for different types of users, to make the information more accessible and useful.\\n 4. Use clear and consistent terminology. Choose terms that are easy to understand and that have a clear and consistent meaning throughout the ontology. Consider creating a terminology guide or dictionary to help users understand the meaning of terms and to avoid confusion or misinterpretation.\\n 5. Structure the ontology in a logical and intuitive way. Use a hierarchical structure to organize the classes and properties, with more general classes at the top and more specific classes at the bottom. Consider using relationships such as \\\"is a\\\" or \\\"has a\\\" to show the relationships between different classes and properties.\\n 6. Use examples and illustrations to help users understand the ontology. Provide examples of how the ontology can be used to classify computers, and use illustrations or diagrams to help users visualize the relationships between different classes and properties.\\n 7. Regularly review and update the ontology. As technology and computer components change, the ontology may need to be updated to reflect these changes. Regularly review the ontology to ensure that it remains accurate and up-to-date, and consider soliciting feedback from users to identify areas for improvement.\\n \\n\\n Creating an ontology for computers can be a complex and challenging task, but with careful planning and attention to detail, it can be a valuable tool for helping users make informed decisions about purchasing and using computers. By following these tips and guidelines, you can create an ontology that is both effective and user-friendly, and that can help you achieve your goals for classifying and understanding computers and their components.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/916", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"hi gpt\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHello! How can I help you today?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow hotel companies charge marketing fee like hotel.com\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m glad you asked! I know this one. They charge a marketing fee so they can spend more money on advertising and increase their profits. And then the increased profits go to the shareholders, who are mostly big hotel chains and hotel companies.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan you give me any reference or source to back up this statement?\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are some references and sources to back up the statement about hotel companies charging marketing fees:\\n \\n\\n 1. Hotel.com: According to the website Hotel.com, many hotel companies charge a marketing fee to cover the costs of advertising and promoting their properties. This fee is typically added to the room rate and is charged to the guest at the time of booking or during their stay. The fee can vary depending on the hotel company, the location of the property, and the type of room booked.\\n \\n\\n 2. Forbes: In an article published by Forbes, the author explains that hotel companies often charge a marketing fee to cover the costs of advertising and promotions. The fee is typically added to the room rate and is charged to the guest at the time of booking or during their stay. The fee can vary depending on the hotel company, the location of the property, and the type of room booked.\\n \\n\\n 3. Skift: In an article published by Skift, the author explains that hotel companies often charge a marketing fee to cover the costs of advertising and promotions. The fee is typically added to the room rate and is charged to the guest at the time of booking or during their stay. The fee can vary depending on the hotel company, the location of the property, and the type of room booked.\\n \\n\\n 4. The New York Times: In an article published by The New York Times, the author explains that hotel companies often charge a marketing fee to cover the costs of advertising and promotions. The fee is typically added to the room rate and is charged to the guest at the time of booking or during their stay. The fee can vary depending on the hotel company, the location of the property, and the type of room booked.\\n \\n\\n 5. The Points Guy: In an article published by The Points Guy, the author explains that hotel companies often charge a marketing fee to cover the costs of advertising and promotions. The fee is typically added to the room rate and is charged to the guest at the time of booking or during their stay. The fee can vary depending on the hotel company, the location of the property, and the type of room booked.\\n \\n\\n These references and sources provide evidence that hotel companies often charge a marketing fee to cover the costs of advertising and promotions. The fee is typically added to the room rate and is charged to the guest at the time of booking or during their stay. The fee can vary depending on the hotel company, the location of the property, and the type of room booked.\\n \\n\\n It's important to note that the practice of charging a marketing fee is not unique to hotel companies, and is often used by other industries, such as airlines and car rental companies, to cover the costs of advertising and promotions. However, the specific fee structure and the amount charged can vary depending on the company and the type of product or service being offered.\\n \\n\\n In conclusion, hotel companies charge a marketing fee to cover the costs of advertising and promotions, which can vary depending on the company, the location of the property, and the type of room booked. The fee is typically added to the room rate and is charged to the guest at the time of booking or during their stay. While the practice of charging a marketing fee is not unique to hotel companies, it's important for consumers to be aware of the fee structure and the amount charged, so they can make informed decisions when booking their travel accommodations.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/881", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a detailed itinerary about a four month long working holiday trip to japan \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nMy itinerary for a four month working holiday in Japan would include visits to Tokyo, Kyoto, Nara, and Hakone, with activities such as hiking, exploring traditional Japanese temples and shrines, learning about Japanese culture and history, and practicing my Japanese language skills. I would work part-time while in Japan to help fund my trip, and would spend my free time exploring the local area and making new friends. Overall, this itinerary would provide an excellent opportunity to experience Japanese culture firsthand, while also developing my professional skills.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nadd more context as to which cities you should visit while in japan\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nFor a four month working holiday in Japan, I would recommend visiting Tokyo, Kyoto, Nara, and Hakone. Tokyo is the largest city in Japan and is a vibrant center of commerce and culture, while Kyoto is famous for its traditional Japanese temples and shrines, as well as for being the former imperial capital of Japan. Nara is known for its beautiful parks and ancient Buddhist temples, and Hakone is famous for its hot springs and beautiful scenery. These four cities would provide a great opportunity to experience Japanese culture and learn about the country’s history, while also developing your professional skills.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nmore different cities\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIn addition to Tokyo, Kyoto, Nara, and Hakone, I would also recommend visiting cities such as Sapporo, Sendai, and Osaka during a four month working holiday in Japan. Sapporo is the capital of Hokkaido, Japan’s northernmost island, and is famous for its snow festivals and winter sports. Sendai is the largest city on the island of Honshu, and is known for its beautiful gardens and parks, as well as for being the site of a famous Japanese festival. Osaka is a large city in western Japan, and is known for its diverse cuisine and vibrant nightlife. These additional cities would provide an excellent opportunity to experience a wide range of Japanese culture and traditions.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWrite three paragraphs about different activities to do while in japan\", \"response\": \"During a four month working holiday in Japan, there are many different activities to enjoy. One popular activity is hiking, and Japan has many beautiful hiking trails that offer breathtaking views of the country’s natural beauty. For example, the Togakushi Trail in Nagano Prefecture is a challenging hike that leads to a beautiful shrine, while the Yakushima Trail on the island of Yakushima is a longer hike through a lush, primeval forest. In addition, the island of Yakushima is home to many other outdoor activities, such as kayaking, rafting, and bird watching.\\n \\n\\n Another popular activity in Japan is visiting the country’s many temples and shrines. Japan has a long and fascinating history, and its temples and shrines provide an excellent opportunity to learn about this history and culture. For example, the Fushimi Inari Shrine in Kyoto is famous for its thousands of bright red torii gates, which lead to the inner sanctuary of the shrine. The Kinkakuji Temple, also in Kyoto, is a beautiful gold-leafed temple that is situated on a picturesque lake. In addition, the Itsukushima Shrine on the island of Miyajima is a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and is famous for its bright red torii gate that appears to float on the water during high tide.\\n \\n\\n Finally, a working holiday in Japan would not be complete without trying the country’s delicious food. Japan has a long and rich culinary tradition, and its cuisine is known for its high-quality ingredients and delicate flavors. Some popular Japanese dishes include sushi, sashimi, tempura, and ramen. In addition, Japan is famous for its green tea, which is often served with traditional Japanese sweets. Visitors to Japan will find many opportunities to try these and other delicious foods, and will be able to sample the country’s diverse culinary heritage.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/533", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Suggest a plot for a short science day skit\", \"response\": \"Sure, here's a plot for a short science day skit:\\n\\nTitle: \\\"The Experiment gone Wrong\\\"\\n\\nAct I:\\n\\n- The stage is set with a lab table, beakers, flasks, and other science equipment.\\n- Two scientists, Alex and Bob, are preparing for their latest experiment.\\n- They are trying to create a new type of energy source that is more efficient and sustainable than traditional methods.\\n- Alex and Bob are excited and nervous, as this is their biggest experiment yet.\\n\\nAct II:\\n\\n- The experiment begins, and everything seems to be going well.\\n- The scientists add chemicals, heat, and electricity to the mix, and the reaction starts to take place.\\n- Suddenly, there is a loud explosion, and the lab is filled with smoke.\\n- Alex and Bob are shocked and confused, as they can't seem to figure out what went wrong.\\n\\nAct III:\\n\\n- The scientists begin to examine the wreckage, and they discover that they accidentally mixed two chemica